stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  [*] --> PENDING: REST create
  PENDING --> OUTBOX_RECORDED: same DB transaction
  OUTBOX_RECORDED --> EVENT_PUBLISHED: publisher receives EventBridge ack
  EVENT_PUBLISHED --> STARTED: SQS starter starts Standard execution
  STARTED --> VALIDATING: idempotency claim in DynamoDB
  VALIDATING --> INVENTORY_CHECK: order payload valid
  INVENTORY_CHECK --> PAYMENT_CHECK: simulated inventory available
  INVENTORY_CHECK --> REJECTED: inventory unavailable
  PAYMENT_CHECK --> INVOICE_GENERATION: simulated payment approved
  PAYMENT_CHECK --> REJECTED: payment declined
  INVOICE_GENERATION --> COMPLETED: PDF in private S3; invoice key and status/version committed together
  COMPLETED --> NOTIFICATION: SNS publish order result
  NOTIFICATION --> SUCCEEDED: SNS publish accepted

  OUTBOX_RECORDED --> PUBLISH_RETRY: EventBridge publish failed
  PUBLISH_RETRY --> OUTBOX_RECORDED: retry with backoff
  STARTED --> RETRYING: transient workflow task failure
  RETRYING --> VALIDATING: retry policy permits
  RETRYING --> FAILED: retry limit exhausted
  EVENT_PUBLISHED --> DLQ: SQS delivery limit exhausted
  DLQ --> OPERATIONS_ALERT: CloudWatch DLQ alarm
  FAILED --> OPERATIONS_ALERT: failure metric and execution details
  REJECTED --> NOTIFICATION: SNS publish rejection result
  SUCCEEDED --> TERMINAL
  TERMINAL --> [*]

  note right of STARTED
    DynamoDB OrderProcessing stores
    execution state and idempotency keys.
    Duplicate SQS deliveries do not create
    duplicate business effects.
  end note
  note right of COMPLETED
    PostgreSQL remains authoritative.
    Every state transition checks expected
    status and increments version.
  end note
